EADING ANSWERS 20.pdf", "sha256": "9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 16, "prompt": "All three ____________ are needed to be adjusted as per the levels of the device\ndeployed.", "sourcePage": 5, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 306, "answer": {"text": "radio-opaque markers", "source": {"id": "offline-9bdadcb787fb1522de2e", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 20.pdf", "sha256": "9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 17, "prompt": "With_________ access sheath is rightly repositioned into the LAA.", "sourcePage": 5, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 403, "answer": {"text": "fluoroscopic guidance", "source": {"id": "offline-9bdadcb787fb1522de2e", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 20.pdf", "sha256": "9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 18, "prompt": "With DOAC being introduced, the scope for the __________ enhanced more.", "sourcePage": 5, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 475, "answer": {"text": "warfarin therapy", "source": {"id": "offline-9bdadcb787fb1522de2e", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 20.pdf", "sha256": "9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 19, "prompt": "The recommended oversizing of the device is in range of___________.", "sourcePage": 5, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 553, "answer": {"text": "10% to 20%", "source": {"id": "offline-9bdadcb787fb1522de2e", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 20.pdf", "sha256": "9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 20, "prompt": "In its final stage, the device will be deployed with", "sourcePage": 5, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 627, "answer": {"text": "unsheathing movement", "source": {"id": "offline-9bdadcb787fb1522de2e", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 20.pdf", "sha256": "9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}], "skills": ["reading"], "recordings": [], "answerSources": [{"id": "offline-9bdadcb787fb1522de2e", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 20.pdf", "sha256": "9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}], "passages": []}, {"id": "d7111cd876822265-p6", "label": "Part B · PART B", "part": "B", "sourceSha256": "d7111cd8768222656d768f016777891aca7bc7cb1042f3ac7796ab80d8bcf807", "pages": [6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11], "questions": [{"number": 1, "prompt": "As per the given notice, one of the major duties include;\nA Care professional will have to look for ways to stop bleeding.\nB It is important to maintain hemodynamic stability.\nC Support cardiac function and circulation.\nNursing care of the heart transplant patient\nNursing care of the heart transplant patient is similar to the care of any cardiac surgery\npatient. Bleeding is a major concern in the early postoperative period. Chest tube\ndrainage is frequently monitored (initially every 15 minutes), as are the cardiac output,\npulmonary artery pressures, and CVP. Cardiac tamponade can develop, presenting as\neither a sudden event or a gradual process. Chest tubes are gently milked (not stripped) as\nneeded to maintain patency. Atrial dysrhythmias are relatively common following cardiac\ntransplant. Temporary pacing wires are placed during surgery because surgical\nmanipulation or postoperative swelling may disrupt the conduction system. Hypothermia\nis induced during surgery; postoperatively, the patient is gradually re-warmed over a 1- to\n2-hour period. Cardiac function is impaired in up to 50% of transplanted hearts during the\nearly postoperative period. Inotropic agents such as low-dose dopamine, dobutamine, or\nmilrinone may be required to bring more stability.", "sourcePage": 6, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "offset": 223}, {"number": 5, "prompt": "According to the information given, what is correct?\nA Only 40% of the household could have afforded the medications.\nB 33% of households in lower middle-income countries managed to have used the\nmediations.\nC 25% of households in upper middle-income countries got access to medications.\nMedication Survey\nIn a survey of 598 communities in 18 countries, the availability of aspirin, β-blockers,\nACEIs, and statins varied widely In the low-income countries, only 1 of 30 rural and\nonly 25 of 32 urban communities had all 4 medications available. The 4 medications\nwere potentially unaffordable for 60% of households in low-income countries.\nAvailability rose to 37% (rural) and 62% (urban) in lower middle-income countries and\n73% (rural) and 80% (urban) in upper middle-income countries. Effective strategies for\ndelivering medications are being developed for LMIC where health system infrastructure\nis underdeveloped.", "sourcePage": 10, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "offset": 0}], "skills": ["reading"], "recordings": [], "answerSources": [{"id": "offline-9bdadcb787fb1522de2e", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 20.pdf", "sha256": "9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}], "passages": []}, {"id": "d7111cd876822265-p12", "label": "Part C · READING 20.pdf", "part": "C", "sourceSha256": "d7111cd8768222656d768f016777891aca7bc7cb1042f3ac7796ab80d8bcf807", "pages": [12, 13, 14, 15, 16, 17, 18, 19, 20], "questions": [{"number": 7, "prompt": "According to paragraph 1, the Zika virus disease is;\nA Common\nB Uncommon\nC Severe disease\nD Without any symptoms", "sourcePage": 13, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 1719, "answer": {"text": "C Severe disease", "source": {"id": "offline-9bdadcb787fb1522de2e", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 20.pdf", "sha256": "9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 8, "prompt": "What does paragraph 2 indicate?\nA How does Zika spread from person to person\nB Modes of transmission of Zika\nC How do people get infected with Zika?\nDA&C", "sourcePage": 14, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "offset": 0}, {"number": 9, "prompt": "What is mentioned in paragraph 3?\nA How do people get infected with Zika?\nB What health problems can result from getting Zika?\nC How microcephaly occurs.\nD Microcephaly and birth defects.", "sourcePage": 14, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 177}, {"number": 10, "prompt": "According to paragraph 5, what is recommended for pregnant women?\nA They should not travel to places where the Zika virus is common.\nB They should talk to their partner before going to Zika-infected places.\nC They should inform their doctor before travelling.\nD Not given", "sourcePage": 14, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 388, "answer": {"text": "D Not given", "source": {"id": "offline-9bdadcb787fb1522de2e", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 20.pdf", "sha256": "9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 11, "prompt": "In paragraph 5, how many methods of prevention from Zika are described?\nA Plenty of prevention measures\nB2\nC3\nD4", "sourcePage": 14, "choices": ["A"], "kind": "question", "offset": 684, "answer": {"text": "C 3", "source": {"id": "offline-9bdadcb787fb1522de2e", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 20.pdf", "sha256": "9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 13, "prompt": "According to paragraph 6, which one of the following statements is true?\nA A woman`s future pregnancies will be at risk if she is infected with the Zika virus.\nB There is no evidence that infected women will not face any complications in future\npregnancies.\nC Any woman who is infected with Zika is advised to wait for six months before\ngetting pregnant.\nDB&C", "sourcePage": 15, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "offset": 177, "answer": {"text": "A A woman`s future pregnancies will be at risk if she is infected with the Zika", "source": {"id": "offline-9bdadcb787fb1522de2e", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 20.pdf", "sha256": "9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 14, "prompt": "According to paragraph 6, which of the following is not true?\nA A woman should wait for six months before they get pregnant if they have\ntraveled to any places with the Zika virus.\nB If the woman has been infected with the Zika virus and has cleared the virus, she is\nlikely to be protected from future Zika infections.\nC In most of the cases, Zika complications may occur in future pregnancies.\nD All above statements are true.\nText 2: Avian Influenza - A Virus Infections in Humans", "sourcePage": 15, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 562, "answer": {"text": "C In most of the cases, Zika complications may occur in future pregnancies.", "source": {"id": "offline-9bdadcb787fb1522de2e", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 20.pdf", "sha256": "9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 15, "prompt": "According to paragraph 1, the virus enters the human body through.\nA The nose\nB The eyes\nC The mouth\nD Contact with an infected bird", "sourcePage": 18, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 0, "answer": {"text": "B The eyes", "source": {"id": "offline-9bdadcb787fb1522de2e", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 20.pdf", "sha256": "9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 16, "prompt": "According to paragraph 1, human infection with avian influenza A virus is;\nA Uncommon\nB Common\nC Rare\nD Frequent in infected places", "sourcePage": 18, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 157, "answer": {"text": "A Uncommon", "source": {"id": "offline-9bdadcb787fb1522de2e", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 20.pdf", "sha256": "9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 17, "prompt": "According to paragraph 2, people may suffer from flu if they have been infected by\nA LPAI\nB HPAI\nC H5N1\nD LPAI H7N9", "sourcePage": 18, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 313, "answer": {"text": "B HPAI", "source": {"id": "offline-9bdadcb787fb1522de2e", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 20.pdf", "sha256": "9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 18, "prompt": "According to paragraph 3, what is not true?\nA A molecular test is performed to see the presence of the virus in the collected\nspecimen.\nB Lab tests are aimed at growing the virus for the right detection purpose.\nC A specimen for testing is usually collected right after the person gets the illness by\ninfection.", "sourcePage": 18, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "offset": 453, "answer": {"text": "D People who have recovered from the illness should also be diagnosed for", "source": {"id": "offline-9bdadcb787fb1522de2e", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 20.pdf", "sha256": "9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 19, "prompt": "According to paragraph 3, the word â€œgargantuanâ€• may mean;\nA Small-scale\nB Trivial\nC Very large\nD Pint-sized", "sourcePage": 19, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 97, "answer": {"text": "C Very large", "source": {"id": "offline-9bdadcb787fb1522de2e", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 20.pdf", "sha256": "9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 20, "prompt": "Which central idea is presented in paragraph 4?\nA Treatment of the avian influenza disease.\nB Effective medications for the viral disease.\nC Research on effective medicine for the avian virus disease.\nD None of the above.", "sourcePage": 19, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 233, "answer": {"text": "A Treatment of the avian influenza disease.", "source": {"id": "offline-9bdadcb787fb1522de2e", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 20.pdf", "sha256": "9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 21, "prompt": "According to paragraph 5, which word may give the meaning of experience?\nA Exposure\nB Expert\nC Intellectualism\nD None of the above", "sourcePage": 19, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 479, "answer": {"text": "A Exposure", "source": {"id": "offline-9bdadcb787fb1522de2e", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 20.pdf", "sha256": "9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}], "skills": ["reading"], "recordings": [], "answerSources": [{"id": "offline-9bdadcb787fb1522de2e", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 20.pdf", "sha256": "9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/9bdadcb787fb1522de2ea8c6ec4f70ec7184f69d82154ae59736d5a913529881.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}], "passages": []}]}
